WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:10.500
ISO/IEC 27018:2025 is focused guidance for protecting PII in public cloud services when the provider acts as a PII processor.

2
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:22.920
The central ideas are role clarity, customer instructions, privacy-specific interpretation of security controls, lifecycle control of PII, transparency, accountability, and evidence.

3
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:44.300
It complements ISO/IEC 27001, ISO/IEC 27002, ISO/IEC 27017, ISO/IEC 27701, and ISO/IEC 29100, but it does not replace them and does not replace legal or contractual analysis.

4
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.940
A defensible implementation begins by obtaining the current standard through an authorized source.

5
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.240
Define the cloud service and organizational scope.

6
00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.540
Identify all PII processing activities.

7
00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:04.320
Determine the role for each activity, including controller, processor, customer, provider, and subprocessor relationships.

8
00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:14.580
Map data flows, storage locations, regions, replicas, backups, telemetry, logs, support systems, and downstream dependencies.

9
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:23.400
Then identify legal, regulatory, contractual, customer, and organization-specific obligations that affect the scoped service.

10
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.240
The next phase is control planning.

11
00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:32.100
Compare existing controls with the applicable guidance without pretending that a generic checklist is enough.

12
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.440
Prioritize gaps by privacy and security risk.

13
00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:49.580
Implement changes in architecture, configuration, procedure, contract language, support processes, incident playbooks, retention rules, deletion behavior, subprocessor governance, and customer documentation.

14
00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:59.280
Assign measurable control ownership so every major safeguard has an owner, configuration, monitoring method, evidence source, exception process, and review cadence.

15
00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.560
Assurance comes from evidence produced by normal operation.

16
00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:23.820
Collect PII inventories, processing records, responsibility matrices, access reviews, privileged-access logs, encryption and key-management records, deletion evidence, incident exercises, notification procedures, training records, audit results, corrective actions, and management reviews.

17
00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.520
Test effectiveness rather than relying on design statements.

18
00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:33.780
A control that exists on paper but is not monitored, reviewed, or evidenced has limited assurance value.

19
00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:39.020
Provider evaluation should be scoped and skeptical in a constructive way.

20
00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:52.160
Review the services, regions, legal entities, audit periods, subservice organizations, exceptions, complementary customer controls, report limitations, evidence freshness, and remediation status.

21
00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.580
ISO develops standards but does not certify organizations.

22
00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:04.760
Certification or independent assurance can be valuable only when the scope and basis of the claim match the processing activity being evaluated.

23
00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:13.900
ISO/IEC 27018 should not be represented as proof that every processing activity complies with every privacy law.

24
00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:41.140
The roadmap is continuous: obtain the standard, define scope, identify PII processing, determine roles, map data and dependencies, identify obligations, assess risk, select controls, implement changes, assign owners, collect evidence, test effectiveness, review provider and subprocessor changes, correct findings, and reassess as services and obligations change.

25
00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:48.600
The outcome learners should carry forward is not merely awareness of ISO/IEC 27018.

26
00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:55.740
It is a practical method for turning cloud privacy guidance into accountable, reviewable, and improvable operations.

27
00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:02.900
A strong closing test is whether the organization can explain its program without leaning on unsupported claims.

28
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:20.680
It should be able to say what edition was used, what services are in scope, what role applies to each processing activity, what obligations influenced the design, what controls operate, what evidence exists, which assurance reports apply, what limitations remain, and how findings are corrected.

29
00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.740
That level of clarity is the real value of the work.

30
00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:28.880
It turns the standard from a reference document into a repeatable operating method.
